Keep a traverse's documented overshoot recovery only when the immutable calculation
authority admits both possible recovery feet cells. A bounded route can then use its
ordinary in-bound cardinal leg without declaring an outside overshoot as success;
the host's physical sweep remains the final backstop for real motion.

